From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GKI KernelSU SUSFS <root>
Date: Mon Jan  1 00:00:00 2026 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fuse: disable MTK blocktag vendor hook entirely

MTK's blocktag vendor hook (BTMTR) emits block_io_start and
block_io_get_result trace calls while holding fiq->lock, risking
deadlock after sync FUSE requests (statfs/getattr). Worse, on
MT6893/lyriq the hook writes to read-only memory on background
requests (fuse_file_put -> flush_bg_queue), panicking the kernel
(Oops, ESR 0x9600004f) and rebooting under container FUSE load.
Disabled for all FUSE requests via if (false), removed by DCE.
FUSE is not block I/O, so no QoS tagging is lost.

Signed-off-by: GKI KernelSU SUSFS <root>
diff --git a/fs/fuse/dev.c b/fs/fuse/dev.c
index d0bf4bc..ebfc006 100644
--- a/fs/fuse/dev.c
+++ b/fs/fuse/dev.c
@@ -236,6 +236,14 @@ __releases(fiq->lock)
 		fuse_len_args(req->args->in_numargs,
 			      (struct fuse_arg *) req->args->in_args);
 	list_add_tail(&req->list, &fiq->pending);
+	/*
+	 * MTK blocktag's block_io_start/block_io_get_result trace calls
+	 * are not safe under fiq->lock and write to read-only memory on
+	 * background requests (panic). Disabled for all FUSE requests;
+	 * FUSE is not block I/O, so no QoS tagging is lost. Panic was
+	 * btag_fuse_queue_request_and_unlock+0x310, ESR 0x9600004f.
+	 */
+	if (false)
 	trace_android_vh_queue_request_and_unlock(&fiq->waitq, sync);
 	fiq->ops->wake_pending_and_unlock(fiq, sync);
 }
